The Windows-specific patches support static builds and MSVC OpenSSL detection.
Applying them on other platforms leaves the MSVC code paths inactive.

FFmpeg uses OpenSSL on all platforms. Non-Windows builds use OpenSSL 3 or later
from Kodi's depends SDK, or the host development installation for native builds.
GPLv3 is enabled on non-Windows builds for compatibility with OpenSSL 3.

Last update and patches refreshed for FFmpeg-n8.0
